# Copy to .env for local development. Every value here is PUBLISHABLE and is
# shipped to the browser in the built bundle -- the anon key is protected by
# RLS, not by secrecy.
#
# Nothing secret belongs in this file or in .env. Server-side credentials
# (SP-API, Keepa, service-role, internal sync secret) live only in Supabase
# edge-function secrets and are never present on a dev machine.

# Read by local scripts that take them from the shell (e.g. the isolation
# test), NOT by the browser build -- Vite only exposes names it is told to.
SUPABASE_URL="https://<project-ref>.supabase.co"
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="<anon key from the Supabase dashboard>"

# Read by the browser build. These must ALSO be set in the hosting project,
# because nothing in the repo supplies them once this file is untracked.
#
# Note the main Supabase client does NOT read these -- src/integrations/supabase/
# client.ts carries the URL and key as literals. What depends on them is the
# handful of places that build their own function URLs (inventory review scan,
# store scan, historical settled sync, the two admin exports). Missing values
# there produce a request to "undefined/functions/v1/..." rather than any
# visible build failure, so verify a build rather than assuming one.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://<project-ref>.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="<project-ref>"
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="<anon key from the Supabase dashboard>"

# VITE_SPAPI_CLIENT_ID was here and has been removed: a repo-wide search finds
# it in no source file. It was inherited from the committed .env this template
# was generated from. Do not reinstate it without a reader.
